From 81e937c8d9f144dfed645abc83604301ee8faa6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:16:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] plugin_api: pixel surface slots for Host API 3

A pixel plugin needs memory it can draw into and AERA can show without a
copy over the control socket.

Add plugin_api/surface: a sealed memfd holding N frame slots of
stride x height ARGB8888, shared with the plugin, and the bookkeeping of
who owns each slot. A presented slot is pending, then latched for the next
refresh, then shown. A pending slot superseded by a newer PRESENT is
released at once; a shown slot is released only when a newer frame
replaces it on screen, so the plugin never draws into a slot being scanned
out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
